chore(v1.1): pin launcher line endings and drop the stray commit-message file

.gitattributes keeps start-local.bat as CRLF and start-local.sh as LF on every
checkout, so a Windows user gets a batch file cmd can parse and a Linux user gets a
script bash can execute. A test asserts the attributes.

Also removes .commitmsg.tmp, which git add -A picked up twice; it held only commit
text and is not part of the release tree.

Tests: 485 passed, 2 skipped (bash-only syntax test skipped on Windows); Ruff clean.
